    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</em></p><p>When this 3-inch metal ball is activated as a Magic action, it races about at great speed, bouncing off walls and defying every attempt to catch it. It stays active for 1 minute or until you deactivate it by speaking a command word within 30 feet of it (no action required). Once used, the ball can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>When you activate the ball, and at the start of each of your turns while it is active, each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking Bludgeoning damage on a failed save. The save DC and the damage depend on the approximate size of the area where the ball is active, as shown on the following table.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Save DC</th><th>Bludgeoning Damage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>15-foot Cube</td><td>18</td><td>6d6 + 5</td></tr><tr><td>30-foot Cube</td><td>17</td><td>4d6 + 4</td></tr><tr><td>50-foot Cube</td><td>15</td><td>2d6 + 2</td></tr><tr><td>100-foot Cube</td><td>14</td><td>1d6 + 1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A nonmagical object that isn’t being worn or carried also takes the damage if it is in the area. In an enclosed area larger than a 100-foot Cube, the ball’s damage is negligible. If the ball is activated in an open area, it flies off in a random direction at 300 feet per round.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-2PsmBPEq10B3CDpD\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Activate</em> dépense l’utilisation du jour ; utilisez ensuite le jet de sauvegarde de la taille de la zone, à l’activation puis au début de chacun de vos tours.</p></section>",
